        "biography": "",
        "appearance": "",
        "notes": "<h5>Tactics</h5><p>A <strong>bodyguard</strong> must be decisive and fast, operating skillfully in close-range combat. They Close the Distance as swiftly as possible, then use Protective Duty to keep their charges safe. In Era 2, a bodyguard may attack with their Boot Pistol before reaching their charge, then swap to their Sidesword to continue the fight. They use their Subdue action as necessary to give their charge a chance to flee. Meanwhile, their Hold the Line feature ensures the bodyguard is di cult to take out of the fight and can stay where they need to be on the battlefield.</p>",
        "role": "rival"
    },
